                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Clockwise is a repetitive (light) horror puzzle game that could leave you frustrated before even finishing the game - and not because it is challenging. You'll navigate a rather \"linear\" game that leaves you running around in circles unable to go backwards one you enter a room, (hence \"Clockwise\"), trying to solve simple riddles or lack of in various of rooms. These rooms are repetitive and half way through the game, you'll start going through them quickly. \n\nThere is no real story and what dialog there is leaves you questioning a lot of different aspects of the game. Perhaps it was intended to be that way to have the player engage in some creative thinking, but does not go far. Aesthetic is alright and compliments the purpose of the game. There is little music in the game and you'll often make a quick glance around to once you hear creaking - nothing to worry about. It's just the house shifting. \n\nThe end of the game can be a little challenging as it doesn't tell you what you are suppose to do. [spoiler]You have to throw books at the picture frame when shield is down and dodge pulses. [/spoiler] It leaves you feeling frustrated that you wasted time, probably missed that one \"secret passage\" achievement, and wondering what the heck that was all about in a unfortunate way.\n\nWhile not an absolute \"trash\" of a game. I would not recommend and unless you are really looking for a game to collect achievements with - find something else to enjoy. There's very little to praise on this game.",
